<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The Measurement Challeng=
e:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The trickiest part is <strong>me=
asuring the impact</strong>. I use a combination of:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Bundle analysis tools</=
strong> (webpack-bundle-analyzer)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Custom metrics</strong>=
 in CI/CD that fail builds if bundle size increases unexpectedly</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Runtime performance mon=
itoring</strong> to correlate bundle size with actual user experience</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">In one project, I discovered tha=
t importing <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-30=
0 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9=
rem]">moment.js</code> incorrectly was adding <strong>67KB of locale files<=
/strong> even though we only needed basic date formatting. The fix was swit=
ching to <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 t=
ext-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem=
]">date-fns</code> with explicit imports, reducing our bundle by <strong>15=
%</strong>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Th=
at's a comprehensive approach! I particularly like your mention of deep imp=
orts and the custom auditing tool. At NAB, we've had similar challenges wit=
h locale files and analytics libraries.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me shift gears to something =
we encounter frequently: <strong>module aggregation patterns</strong>. We h=
ave a large codebase with many shared utilities, and we use barrel exports =
extensively for developer experience. However, I suspect this might be harm=
ing our Tree Shaking effectiveness. Can you walk me through the problems wi=
th barrel exports and how you'd recommend structuring module exports in a l=
arge-scale application?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is <strong>exactly</strong> the type of problem that can silently destroy =
Tree Shaking effectiveness in large applications! Barrel exports are a clas=
sic case where <strong>developer experience conflicts with bundle optimizat=
ion</strong>, and most teams don't realize the impact until it's too late.<=
/p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The Barrel Export Proble=
m:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me illustrate with a common =
pattern I see in enterprise codebases:</p>
