<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Real-world impact predic=
tion</strong>: Based on similar optimizations, I expect:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Bundle size reduction</=
strong>: 85-95% for typical use cases</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Load time improvement</=
strong>: 200-400ms on 3G networks</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Tree Shaking effectiven=
ess</strong>: Increase from ~15% to ~90%</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key insight is that <strong>=
object aggregation patterns are Tree Shaking killers</strong> - they force =
bundlers to include entire dependency graphs rather than just the code you =
actually use.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ou=
tstanding analysis! Your systematic approach and the migration strategy sho=
w real production experience. I particularly appreciate how you've balanced=
 the technical optimization with practical deployment concerns.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me dive deeper into one aspe=
ct: <strong>dynamic imports and lazy loading</strong>. You mentioned using =
dynamic imports in the API module. At NAB, we're dealing with a complex sce=
nario where we have different API clients for different business domains (r=
etail banking, business banking, wealth management), and each has substanti=
al dependencies.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Can you show me how you'd archit=
ect a <strong>dynamic loading system</strong> that maintains Tree Shaking b=
enefits while providing a clean developer experience? Also, I'm curious abo=
ut the <strong>performance implications</strong> - when does the overhead o=
f dynamic imports outweigh the bundle size benefits?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Exce=
llent question! <strong>Dynamic imports with Tree Shaking optimization</str=
ong> is one of the most powerful patterns for large enterprise applications=
, but it requires careful architectural planning to avoid <strong>performan=
ce pitfalls</strong>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>=F0=9F=8F=97=EF=B8=8F En=
terprise API Client Architecture:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me design a system that hand=
les NAB's multi-domain requirements:</p>
