<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Bottom Line for NAB:</st=
rong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Use dynamic imports</st=
rong> for domain-specific clients (60-90% bundle reduction)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Implement predictive pr=
eloading</strong> for frequently accessed domains</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Monitor the 65ms overhe=
ad</strong> - acceptable for most business flows</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Keep core APIs static</=
strong> - authentication, routing, error handling</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The <strong>sweet spot</strong> =
is typically modules &gt;50KB used by &lt;30% of users - perfect for your m=
ulti-domain API clients scenario.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Br=
illiant! Your performance breakpoints and the decision matrix are exactly t=
he kind of systematic thinking we value at NAB. The real-world results from=
 your retail banking app are compelling evidence.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Now let's tackle our final chall=
enge - this is where I really want to see your <strong>problem-solving proc=
ess</strong> in action.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>CODING CHALLENGE:</stron=
g></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">I'm going to give you a <strong>=
realistic but complex Tree Shaking scenario</strong> that combines multiple=
 issues we've discussed. You'll need to both analyze and code the solution.=
 Here's the situation:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">We have a legacy <strong>notific=
ations system</strong> at NAB that various teams use. It's currently causin=
g massive bundle bloat, but it's critical infrastructure that can't be take=
n offline. The system has grown organically and now includes:</p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Push notifications</str=
ong> (web push, mobile push)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Email notifications</st=
rong> (transactional, marketing)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>SMS notifications</stro=
ng> (OTP, alerts)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>In-app notifications</s=
trong> (toasts, modals, banners)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Analytics tracking</str=
ong> for all notification types</li>
</ol>
